<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otto Henry, Elector Palatine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1502">1502</a>–<a href="/years/1559">1559</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Ottheinrich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otto Henry, known in German as Ottheinrich, was ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palatinate-neuburg">Palatinate-Neuburg</a> from 1505 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elector-palatine">Elector Palatine</a> from 1556. He introduced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neuburg-an-der-donau">Neuburg</a> in 1542 and was a lavish patron of art and building, rebuilding the palace at Neuburg and adding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> Ottheinrich Building to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg-castle">Heidelberg Castle</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otto-henry-elector-palatine.jpg" alt="Otto Henry, Elector Palatine" width="320" height="403" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georg Pencz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Georg_Pencz_001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
